01:12:46,880 --> 01:12:50,370
I guess it's more of
an opinion question.

1432
01:12:50,370 --> 01:12:54,290
As you write your learning
outcomes I think in some ways

1433
01:12:54,290 --> 01:12:57,230
it's better to be specific
about the real world problems

1434
01:12:57,230 --> 01:12:58,700
that they're going to attack.

1435
01:12:58,700 --> 01:13:02,130
Because I've seen that on
syllabuses all the time.

1436
01:13:02,130 --> 01:13:04,090
I'm very excited about it.

1437
01:13:04,090 --> 01:13:06,540
I think it's a way to
teach people in your class.

1438
01:13:06,540 --> 01:13:10,460
It's going to help them know
what tools they're getting.

1439
01:13:10,460 --> 01:13:11,460
JANET RANKIN: Right.

1440
01:13:11,460 --> 01:13:13,650
I mean, real world
problems in particular

1441
01:13:13,650 --> 01:13:19,590
really do kind of encapsulate a
whole pile of hopes and dreams.

1442
01:13:19,590 --> 01:13:21,600
So it may help to be a
little more specific.

1443
01:13:21,600 --> 01:13:24,630
You can use it in your
learning outcomes,

1444
01:13:24,630 --> 01:13:27,450
but then maybe describe
it in a little more detail

1445
01:13:27,450 --> 01:13:32,280
in your syllabus, the kinds
of real world problems,

1446
01:13:32,280 --> 01:13:34,170
or why we care about
real world problems.

1447
01:13:34,170 --> 01:13:35,140
They're messy.

1448
01:13:35,140 --> 01:13:36,750
They're ill-defined.

1449
01:13:36,750 --> 01:13:39,310
What about them is so important?

1450
01:13:39,310 --> 01:13:43,530
What about them is so important?

1451
01:13:43,530 --> 01:13:45,420
Try to minimize the buzz words.

1452
01:13:45,420 --> 01:13:47,859
But at some level, they may
not know about something

1453
01:13:47,859 --> 01:13:49,900
until they're completely
through with the course,

1454
01:13:49,900 --> 01:13:51,316
and you may have
to use that word.

1455
01:13:51,316 --> 01:13:53,550
So there's a bit of a balance.

1456
01:13:53,550 --> 01:13:54,990
What I'm going to
do before, I'll

1457
01:13:54,990 --> 01:13:56,880
